individual or entity that installs or uses the Software ("you"). By installing,
activating, or using the Software you agree to this Agreement. If you do not
agree, do not install or use the Software. If you accept this Agreement on
behalf of an organization, you represent that you have the authority to bind
that organization, and "you" refers to that organization.

**Please read the sections in bold with particular care. They limit Reallysec's
warranties and liability and restrict how you may use the Software.**

## 1. Definitions

- **"Software"** means RST Elastic AI Copilot in object-code form as delivered
  by Reallysec, including container images, deployment files, compiled
  feature modules, documentation, and any updates Reallysec provides.
- **"Documentation"** means the user and installation guides Reallysec publishes
  for the Software at https://reallysec.com/docs.
- **"License"** means the license key or license file issued by Reallysec that
  specifies your edition, feature set, node count, user count, and term.
- **"Edition"** means the Community, Professional, or Enterprise edition, or a
  trial. The Professional and Enterprise editions and trials are stated in your
  License; the Community Edition is the Software used without a License.
- **"Order"** means the quotation, purchase order, or other document under which
  you acquired the License.
- **"Your Data"** means the logs, alerts, and other data that the Software
  processes on your behalf.

## 2. License Grant

Subject to this Agreement and payment of the applicable fees, Reallysec grants
you a non-exclusive, non-transferable, non-sublicensable license, for the term
stated in your License, to install and use the Software for your internal
business operations, on no more nodes and for no more users than your License
permits, and limited to the features of your Edition. Your employees and contractors may use the
Software on your behalf; you are responsible for their compliance with this
Agreement.

A trial License grants the same rights for evaluation only, for the trial period
stated in the License.

Without a License, Reallysec grants you the same license free of charge and
without a fixed term, limited to the features of the Community Edition, one
user, and one node. Reallysec may change the features of the Community Edition
in later versions of the Software.

## 3. Restrictions

**You must not, and must not permit any third party to:**

1. **move, change, disable, or circumvent the license key functionality, or
   remove or obscure any functionality protected by the license key;**
2. **decrypt, decompile, disassemble, or reverse engineer the compiled feature
   modules or any other part of the Software, except to the extent applicable
   law expressly permits despite this restriction;**
3. **provide the Software to third parties as a hosted or managed service, or
   otherwise give third parties access to a substantial set of its features;**
4. **sell, rent, lease, lend, sublicense, distribute, or otherwise transfer the
   Software or the License, except as Reallysec agrees in writing;**
5. **share one License across more nodes, users, hosts, or organizations
   than it permits;**
6. **remove, alter, or obscure any copyright, trademark, license, or other
   notice in the Software;**
7. **use the Software in violation of applicable law, including export control
   and data protection laws.**

## 4. Ownership

The Software is licensed, not sold. Reallysec and its licensors retain all right,
title, and interest in and to the Software, including all intellectual property
rights. All rights not expressly granted in this Agreement are reserved.

If you provide suggestions or feedback about the Software, Reallysec may use them
without restriction or obligation to you.

## 5. Third-Party Components

The Software includes third-party and open-source components, listed in the
THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES file delivered with the Software. Each is licensed under its
own terms, which govern your use of that component. Nothing in this Agreement
limits your rights under those licenses.

## 6. Data

The Software runs in your environment. Your Data stays under your control, and
you are responsible for it, including under applicable data protection laws.

Apart from destinations you configure yourself (such as your Elasticsearch and
Kibana, notification channels and audit-forwarding targets), the Software sends
data outside your environment only as listed here:

- **License service.** When a License is activated online and on each periodic
  heartbeat, the Software sends Reallysec's license service
  (license.reallysec.com) the license identifier, the product identifier and
  version, the host fingerprint (a hash derived from machine identifiers), and
  the `cluster_uuid` and version of the connected Elasticsearch cluster. Offline
  activation, where your Edition includes it, sends nothing.
- **Verification-failure report.** If a downloaded release or content pack fails
  signature or checksum verification, the Software sends the license service the
  license identifier, the product version and the reason for the failure.
- **Update checks.** Once a day the Software downloads public release and
  content-pack files from GitHub Releases. These requests send no customer data
  beyond what any HTTP request carries.
- **Language models.** The Software sends prompts and query results, which may
  include portions of Your Data, to the language-model endpoints you configure,
  subject to the field masking mode you select, and to no other destination.
  Those endpoints are provided by you or your chosen provider under their own
  terms; Reallysec does not receive that data.

Nothing sent to Reallysec or to GitHub under this Section includes the contents
of your logs, alerts or queries.

## 7. Updates, Support, and Preview Features

Reallysec may provide updates during the term of your License. Support, service
levels, and maintenance are provided only as set out in your Order or a separate
support agreement.

Features that the Software or the Documentation marks as preview, beta, or
experimental are provided for evaluation. Reallysec may change or remove them
at any time, and Section 9.1 does not apply to them.

## 8. Usage Verification

At Reallysec's written request, no more than once in any twelve (12) month
period, you will provide within thirty (30) days a written statement, signed by
an authorized representative, of the number of nodes on which the Software is
installed, the number of users, and the Edition in use. If the statement shows use beyond your
License, you will pay the applicable fees for the excess use under Reallysec's
then-current price list.

## 9. Warranty

### 9.1 Limited warranty

For a paid License, Reallysec warrants that for ninety (90) days from the date
the License is first issued, the Software will perform substantially as
described in the Documentation. If it does not, and you notify Reallysec within
that period, Reallysec will at its option correct the Software or refund the
fees you paid for the nonconforming Software, in which case your License ends.
**This is your sole and exclusive remedy for breach of this warranty.** The
warranty does not apply to the Community Edition, trial Licenses, preview features, or problems caused
by modification, misuse, or an environment the Documentation does not support.

### 9.2 Disclaimer

**Except for Section 9.1, and to the maximum extent permitted by law, the
Software is provided "as is" and "as available", without warranties of any
kind, express or implied, including warranties of merchantability, fitness for
a particular purpose, and non-infringement. Reallysec does not warrant that the
Software will be error-free or uninterrupted, or that it will detect, prevent,
or mitigate any security incident. Output generated with language models may
be inaccurate and must be reviewed before you rely on it. The Software supports,
and does not replace, your own security controls, monitoring, and professional
judgment.**

## 10. Limitation of Liability

**To the maximum extent permitted by law, Reallysec is not liable for any
indirect, incidental, special, consequential, or punitive damages, or for any
loss of profits, revenue, data, or business, even if advised of the possibility
